WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.736 --> 00:00:02.480
(whistle blows)

00:00:02.480 --> 00:00:04.730
(shouting)

00:00:09.790 --> 00:00:12.353
- [Man] We've got a big mix
of everybody in the club.

00:00:13.750 --> 00:00:16.680
Gay, straight, bi, whatever,

00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:18.067
and everyone is welcomed.

00:00:18.067 --> 00:00:20.933
The club has completely changed my life.

00:00:25.105 --> 00:00:27.605
(piano music)

00:00:29.030 --> 00:00:32.633
- [Woman] BMW proudly
supports the LGBTQ community.

00:00:36.882 --> 00:00:39.299
(chattering)

00:00:45.142 --> 00:00:48.142
(players shouting)

00:00:49.297 --> 00:00:50.520
- [Robert] The challenges that

00:00:50.520 --> 00:00:55.340
the people were facing in the
1990s were fairly standard.

00:00:55.340 --> 00:00:58.090
There was an automatic
link between being gay

00:00:58.090 --> 00:00:59.800
and being pedophile.

00:00:59.800 --> 00:01:02.280
You certainly couldn't be macho.

00:01:02.280 --> 00:01:04.790
When I heard about the formation

00:01:04.790 --> 00:01:06.860
of the world's first gay rugby club,

00:01:06.860 --> 00:01:08.520
I thought I just gotta join in

00:01:08.520 --> 00:01:10.381
and help in whatever way I can.

00:01:10.381 --> 00:01:13.768
(players shouting)

00:01:13.768 --> 00:01:16.500
- [Matt] I think Kings Cross
Steelers was the first gay

00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:19.579
and inclusive rugby club founded in 1995.

00:01:19.579 --> 00:01:20.727
(light switch clicks)

00:01:20.727 --> 00:01:23.620
And we currently have 250 active members.

00:01:23.620 --> 00:01:26.490
Our club is made up of gay, bisexual,

00:01:26.490 --> 00:01:28.260
and straight guys who are all here to play

00:01:28.260 --> 00:01:29.700
and enjoy rugby together.

00:01:29.700 --> 00:01:32.435
There's many guys who self
exclude themselves in sports.

00:01:32.435 --> 00:01:34.650
Don't want to take part at school,

00:01:34.650 --> 00:01:36.230
who then want to get back into a sport

00:01:36.230 --> 00:01:40.243
in their adult years and need
a social group in the society.

00:01:41.380 --> 00:01:44.090
- [Matthew] Well, I've
wanted to get into rugby

00:01:44.090 --> 00:01:46.000
and something a lot my family have played,

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:49.930
but I wasn't too comfortable
joining one of the teams

00:01:49.930 --> 00:01:51.210
back at (mumbles).

00:01:51.210 --> 00:01:52.160
(players shouting)

00:01:52.160 --> 00:01:54.200
I wouldn't feel as comfortable

00:01:54.200 --> 00:01:58.450
joining a club that doesn't
label itself as inclusive

00:01:58.450 --> 00:02:00.720
because you've got that little niggle

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:01.840
in the back of your head,

00:02:01.840 --> 00:02:04.240
like will they accept me for being gay?

00:02:04.240 --> 00:02:05.290
Will they not?

00:02:05.290 --> 00:02:09.050
Whereas, here, they all very accepting

00:02:09.050 --> 00:02:11.563
and I know that it won't be an issue.

00:02:12.880 --> 00:02:15.520
I thought I would just
be here to play the sport

00:02:15.520 --> 00:02:18.480
in an open and friendly environment.

00:02:18.480 --> 00:02:22.090
Instead, the club has
become another family.

00:02:22.090 --> 00:02:24.450
Being in an inclusive
environment and (mumbles)

00:02:24.450 --> 00:02:25.723
it's just great.

00:02:27.630 --> 00:02:28.800
(violin music)

00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:33.330
- [Robert] From, six
people in November 1995,

00:02:34.490 --> 00:02:37.980
and a small committee, and
not being able to form a team,

00:02:37.980 --> 00:02:41.400
through to having Steelers
fielding up to six teams

00:02:41.400 --> 00:02:42.714
in any given time.

00:02:42.714 --> 00:02:44.130
(players chattering)

00:02:44.130 --> 00:02:46.250
It's a wonderful pleasure.

00:02:46.250 --> 00:02:48.220
I want, and everybody in the club

00:02:48.220 --> 00:02:52.760
wants, people to enjoy playing
rugby at whatever level,

00:02:52.760 --> 00:02:55.037
but at the same time, being able to say,

00:02:55.037 --> 00:02:56.950
"I'm gay," and it doesn't matter.

00:02:56.950 --> 00:03:01.950
Society has changed so much
over the last 20 years,

00:03:02.610 --> 00:03:05.480
and I just like to think
that we as a rugby club

00:03:05.480 --> 00:03:07.940
have contributed in
some small way to them.

00:03:09.862 --> 00:03:12.695
(music fades out)

